SOA-ESPS Platform Hybrid Licensing Matrix
===============================================================================

This project does not use a single monolithic license. It operates under an
Open-Core / Restricted Modules hybrid licensing model to allow community
contributions to the core framework while protecting proprietary operational logic.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. OPEN-CORE MODULES (Apache License 2.0)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following core infrastructure, utility starters, and standard business
domain modules are licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

  - api-gateway/
  - config/
  - eureka-service/
  - kafka-starter/
  - core/
  - common-functional/
  - auth-service/
  - profile-service/
  - payments-service/
  - quotes-service/
  - documents-service/
  - notes-service/
  - scheduler-service/
  - camunda/
  - data-process/
  - msg-process/

You are free to use, modify, distribute, and commercially exploit the modules
listed above under the terms and conditions of the Apache 2.0 License.
The full text of the Apache 2.0 License can be found at:
https://apache.org

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. PROTECTED INTELLIGENCE & ORCHESTRATION MODULES (CC BY-NC 4.0)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following high-value enterprise routing, stateful streaming, and core
intelligence modules are strictly restricted:

  - coordinator/
  - aggregator/

These specific modules are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-
NonCommercial 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC 4.0).

Under this license:
  - You MAY NOT use these specific modules or their derivatives for commercial
    purposes, production enterprise deployments, or generating revenue.
  - You may copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format, and
    remix, transform, and build upon the material for non-commercial use only,
    provided appropriate credit is given.

To view a copy of this license, visit:
http://creativecommons.org
Or send a letter to Creative Commons, PO Box 1866, Mountain View, CA 94042, USA.

